WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.901
-Our next guest
is a talented actor you know

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.734
from his work in films
such as "Y tu mamá también,"

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.467
"The Motorcycle Diaries,"
and "Coco,"

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:09.234
and shows such as
"Mozart in the Jungle"
and "Station Eleven."

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.400
His latest project, "Cassandro,"
is available now on Prime Video.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.634
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.868
♪♪

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.701
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.100
[ Crowd chanting in Spanish ]

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.067
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:28.868
-[ Shouting Spanish ]

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.968
[Chanting "Cassandro"]

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:45.033
Cassandro! Cassandro!

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.567
Cassandro! Cassandro!

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.834
-Please welcome back to the show
Gael García Bernal, everybody!

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:59.801
♪♪

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:06.968
♪♪

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.234
Welcome back, Gael!
-Yes. Thank you so much.

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:12.167
It's so nice to be here again.
-This is a film about a world

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.834
I will admit
not knowing much about.

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:16.467
This is lucha libre wrestling.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.400
Tell us about exactly
what that means.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.200
-I'm surprised --
You never played that

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.501
with your friends, you know?

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:23.167
-We did, like, world wrestling,

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.868
but not the sort of,
yes, the Mexican style.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:27.367
-The Mexican style. Okay, okay.

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:30.834
So it's, uh -- Lucha libre.
It's, uh, wrestling.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.901
Uh, the translation
is, like, "free wrestling."

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.901
So it's free.

00:01:35.901 --> 00:01:37.701
It's very much
you can do anything.

00:01:37.701 --> 00:01:40.501
It's, uh --
It's got two ramifications

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:41.868
that are very specific.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.801
You know, like, sort of
the teams, you know?

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:46.734
It's técnicos, technicians,

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:50.334
and the rudos,
the rude ones, and --

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:52.367
Or the rough ones. Sorry.
The rough ones.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.767
That would be the translation..
And, eh, it's the same.

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.334
And they, uh, you know --
there's many strands there,

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.567
where one of them
is the exoticos.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.067
-Okay.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:06.901
-Which are, like, the campy,
uh, wrestlers, you know,

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:10.400
and, uh, Cassandro,
amongst his contemporaries --

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.000
Cassandro is the character
I interpret in the film.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.834
Uh, amongst his contemporaries,

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:18.434
they were the first ones
to subvert, more or less,

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:20.501
the notion that people
had about exoticos

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:23.367
because they came out,
uh, openly gay,

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:26.334
and, uh, people started
to support them

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.901
and people started to make them
want to win and, uh --

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.501
And, yeah. Yeah...

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:34.334
See the movie. See the movie.
See the movie.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:38.100
-So, Cassandro
is the wrestling name

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.901
of a real person called Saúl.
-Yes.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:43.901
-And, um, were you aware
of him growing up?

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:46.868
Was he sort of famous enough
to be on your radar?

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.934
-Well, he was -- He came
a little bit afterwards.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.033
You know, as a kid,

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:55.267
I mean, I was watching,
uh, lucha libre on the TV,

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.601
and I saw many wrestlers

00:02:57.601 --> 00:03:00.634
like Atlantis, Octagon,
Rayo de Jalisco.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:02.601
I mean, amazing,
like, legends, no?

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.300
Uh, and Cassandro
came a little bit after.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.701
You know,
because there's a point

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:07.834
where you get a little bit
embarrassed of watching the...

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:09.100
-Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:12.701
So, uh, yeah. Cassandro came
a little bit afterwards.

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:15.267
-You did get to meet
the real Cassandro.

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.601
-Of course!
-Uh, there you are.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.467
-Yeah, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:19.667
Yeah.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.601
-He must have been, uh --

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.334
I would imagine
he was so excited

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:25.067
that you were
all taking the time

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.534
to tell a story like this.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:28.400
-He was very excited, yeah,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.667
and, you know, just delighted
that we would also take on

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:35.767
the fact that, you know,
Saúl created Cassandro,

00:03:35.767 --> 00:03:38.968
created this character
in order to find himself,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:41.133
you know, in order
to see all the dimensions

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:43.300
of who he could be.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.567
And that led him in the road
to discovery, you know?

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:49.534
He was very happy,
I think, of what we did --

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:53.100
is that we also created
our own Cassandro,

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:58.167
and, uh, it took me on a path
of discovery, as well.

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.267
And I think you can
tell that in the movie.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.834
It has that kind of, like --
that kind of, you know,

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.534
just a lot of nirvana moments,
you know,

00:04:05.534 --> 00:04:06.934
of fascination.

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:09.734
And also allowed me
to play a luchador,

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.901
you know, that as a kid,
I used to trash my room

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:13.267
with my friends and my brother.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.868
You know, we used to --
And, uh --

00:04:14.868 --> 00:04:16.968
And now I was doing it for real
in the ring.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:19.267
-He probably appreciated not
just that you told his story,

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.767
but you --
you took it seriously.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.601
You tried to
get into wrestling shape.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.167
Is this accurate?
-Yeah.

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:26.033
-Did you enjoy the training?

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.067
-I enjoyed -- Okay.
So, at the beginning, it was --

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.400
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you for your honesty.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.667
We all know where this is going.

00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.834
-Everything -- Like all stories,
it begins well.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:37.367
-Yeah.
-It begins me eating a lot

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.801
and gaining a lot of weight

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:42.434
and, you know, doing a lot of,
uh, strength exercises,

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.934
you know, calisthenics
and those kind of things.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:48.834
And then -- then two months
before starting to shoot,

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.801
I started to do
the wrestling training.

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:53.434
-Yeah.
-And that, uh -- Ah.

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:56.300
That's just like --

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.334
I mean, as a warmup,
for example,

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:02.033
you have to do
100, like, dead falls

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.801
to the ground,
you know, like "tlack!"

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:06.000
Yes? Yes. Oh-ho. Yeah?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.033
Yeah, because you have to learn
how to fall.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.767
-Right.
-You know? And, uh --

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:12.334
And that's just to begin with,
and that's just the warmup.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:14.968
And if you were like one minute
late, they would come --

00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:17.133
All the wrestlers
that you're training with,

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.334
they would come
and rush towards you

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:20.901
and hit you as hard as you can,

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.367
and you had to fall
and go back again on top.

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.133
And then another person.
Dah! Dah-dah!

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:27.501
And obviously all of them
are bigger than me.

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:29.000
And, you know, it was like...

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.033
-And nobody at any point
stepped in and said,

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.334
"This is the star of the movie.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.300
You leave this poor man alone."

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.300
-Oh. I think in the wrestling
world and in Mexico,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.868
you would say that,
they would hit me even more.

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.267
You know what I'm saying?
So it's like, "No, no.

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.634
He's just train--
He's just training here."

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:49.000
-Did you do -- Was there
anything you had to do,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.400
any sort of physical stunt
where you thought to yourself --

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.367
Because I'm older than you,
but not by a lot.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.567
And there are certain things
I do now where I think,

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:56.968
"Oh, I wasn't ready for that."

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:58.968
Was there any moment
where you were like,

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:00.934
"What am I doing here?"
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:06:00.934 --> 00:06:03.734
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
But the good thing is that --

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.701
I mean, we shot this
with our own --

00:06:05.701 --> 00:06:07.734
with our film family, you know?

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.234
So, the stunt coordinator
is called Balo Bucio,

00:06:10.234 --> 00:06:11.901
and he's fantastic.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:16.534
And he was the interlocutor
with a wrestling organization

00:06:16.534 --> 00:06:18.100
that we worked with, which is...

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.367
And they were really kind
and very giving.

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:23.667
And they -- From the beginning,
they were like,

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:25.667
"No, you can do this.
You can do this."

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:29.234
And I was like, "I --
No, I can't. I can't do that."

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:30.534
They were like,
"Yeah, you'll manage.

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:31.868
You'll manage to do this."

00:06:31.868 --> 00:06:33.868
And indeed I managed

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:37.734
to do all of the stunts
except one -- except two.

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:40.367
But one very, very clear,

00:06:40.367 --> 00:06:42.033
which is called
the Cassandro Bomb.

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:43.667
-Okay.
-Not even Cassandro

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.434
is allowed to do it
because it's illegal, you know?

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:46.734
So it's like --
-What is --

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:48.334
Now you have to explain it.

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:50.167
What's an illegal
Cassandro Bomb?

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:53.367
-Oh, man. I, um -- I'd have to
show it, but then...

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:55.000
-No, no, no.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:58.100
-There wouldn't be a witness
to talk about it like that.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.667
-We're like,
"We're sorry Gael died,

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:02.067
um, but do see his movie."

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:03.968
Hey. Thanks for being here.
It is a really special film.

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:05.467
And it's so nice
to see you again.

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.400
-Thank you so much.
-Gael García Bernal, everybody.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.234
"Cassandro" is streaming now
on Prime Video.

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:11.634
Stick around. We'll be right
back with more "Late Night."

